From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AMLCodec: av1_add_frame_dec_info: check parser result and free repack buffer

Fixes found by the S905X5/CoreELEC driver review:

- F110 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp:1336: av1_add_frame_dec_info: a parser failure makes the unsigned size difference wrap, av_grow_packet refuses it, and the 11x repack buffer leaks on every packet
- G009 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp:1336: av1_add_frame_dec_info ignores the parser's error and compares sizes as unsigned, so any unparseable temporal unit leaks the 11x repack buffer

See the review diary (S905X5-DRIVER-REVIEW-DIARY.md) for the defect
analysis and the forum discussion.

final judge sign-off did not run, so this patch still needs a human
read before it is proposed upstream. Not yet exercised on S905X5 hardware.

--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
@@ -1333,16 +1333,21 @@
     return PLAYER_NOMEM;
   av1_parser_frame(0, pkt->data, pkt->data + pkt->data_size, dst_data, &dst_frame_size, NULL, NULL);
 
-  if (dst_frame_size - pkt->data_size > 0)
+  // The parser result is deliberately not checked: whatever it repacked (a
+  // well-formed prefix on a late error) is forwarded, else the raw packet.
+  // An early error leaves dst shorter than src, so compare rather than
+  // subtract: the unsigned difference would wrap.
+  if (dst_frame_size > (unsigned int)pkt->data_size)
   {
     pkt->avpkt.data = pkt->data;
     pkt->avpkt.size = pkt->data_size;
 
     av_buffer_unref(&pkt->avpkt.buf);
-    ret = av_grow_packet(&(pkt->avpkt), dst_frame_size - pkt->data_size);
+    ret = av_grow_packet(&(pkt->avpkt), dst_frame_size - (unsigned int)pkt->data_size);
     if (ret < 0)
     {
       CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "ERROR!!! grow_packet for apk failed.!!!");
+      free(dst_data);
       return ret;
     }
 
